module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_string_literal_attests_an_emitted_reference

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data a_string_literal_attests_an_emitted_reference: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_string_literal_attests_an_emitted_reference" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a string literal attests an emitted reference: a gate that must decide whether a name is SPELLED IN EMITTED CODE reads the emitted text whole, so a name that appears only inside a string literal -- prose the program carries as data -- passes as though the code paths into it. The Rust emitter's reference-derived use-line pass (v1.compiler.emit_rust reference_derived_use_line_plan) admits a proposed candidate only when its name is among the emitted source's identifier tokens; that attestation exists to reject misproposed candidates, and a prose mention defeated it.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-09-24 by the Pkg7e emitted-workspace plan (v2.workflow.emitted_crate_workspace), whose edge merge refused with EmitterReverseEdge std_content_hash -> v2_std_node. std.content_hash's grounding note names `v2.std.node.Hash`; a candidate `Hash` (v2.std.node declares `type Hash = Fnv1a64Structural`, an alias of std.content_hash's own type) passed the token gate on that prose, and std_content_hash.rs emitted `pub use crate::v2_std_node::\{Hash\};` -- used by nothing, harmless in one crate, and a reverse edge in any partition because v2.std.node imports std.content_hash.",

    "REPAIR at the gate, the earliest link that could not be justified: rust_code_outside_string_literals removes escaped backslashes and quotes, splits on the remaining quote characters and keeps the segments outside literals, and the emitted-token set is built from that. Measured: over a closure entering at v2.std.node the use-line is present before and absent after; across the whole seed the second generation drops eleven use-lines from six mirrors (v1.compiler.emit, emit_rust, infer, trait_derive_emit, gunbc occurrence_binding_parser_walk, and one claim module), every one a name that occurs in that module only inside a string literal; the seed compiles without them, and the following generation is a fixed point.",

    "RUNG: mitigatable -- the partition's typed EmitterReverseEdge refusal is what exposed it, and the multi-crate build is what would fail. ATTAINABLE CEILING: structurally guaranteed. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, at capability grain: use-lines derived from the EMITTED REFERENCE SET the renderers return (the stall gunbc.guarantee_stall emitted_inline_crate_path_edges_unreturned_stall names that capability), sufficient for no text gate to exist at all.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
